# NFR3 structural check (issue #2548's Testing item 8): SourcePath is
# recorded for the audit trail only (import_completion.go's own doc
# comment) -- nothing in this package ever opens the file it names. No
# database needed: this reads the package's own source file back
# (declared as `data` below) and asserts the absence of any
# os.Open/os.ReadFile/ioutil.ReadFile call, so a future change that adds a
# file-read keyed on SourcePath is caught without Docker or Postgres. Part
# of `bazel test //...` (no "manual"/"integration" tag) -- as of this
# change, a repo-wide grep confirms import_completion.go and
# krill/importer/importer.go are the only two files that reference
# SourcePath at all; see importer's own
# TestNFR3_ImporterSourceNeverOpensSourcePath for the other half.
go_test(
    name = "import_completion_nfr3_test",
    srcs = ["import_completion_nfr3_test.go"],
    data = ["import_completion.go"],
)

# NFR2/LB3 structural check (issue #2685's Testing item 5): a status
